WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.880
Welcome to Sprint Three.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:06.403
This is where your Problem Frame
meets the people who experience it.

3
00:00:06.418 --> 00:00:09.520
Your own view matters, and it
is only part of the picture.

4
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.526
Stakeholders can show you pressures,
constraints, and perspectives

5
00:00:15.541 --> 00:00:16.803
you haven't seen yet.

6
00:00:16.818 --> 00:00:20.790
In this sprint, listening
helps you test your frame.

7
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.281
Make room for people's actual
experience, and keep evidence separate

8
00:00:25.296 --> 00:00:27.370
from what you're still inferring.

9
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.910
Artificial intelligence can help
you prepare, but it cannot replace

10
00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:36.145
their input. By the end,
you'll have a frame grounded

11
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.249
in real conversations, with a clearer
sense of what changed and what

12
00:00:40.264 --> 00:00:44.250
remains uncertain. Let's hear
what other people can teach us.
